me>Goldstein</surname><given-names>AO</given-names></name><name><surname>Westbrook</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Howell</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Fischer</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hospital efforts in smoking control: Remaining barriers and challenges</article-title><source>J. Fam. Pract</source><year>1992</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>729</fpage><lpage>734</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1593247</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19-ijerph-06-00246"><label>19.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nagle</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Schofield</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Redman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Smoking on hospital grounds and the impact of outdoor smoke-free zones</article-title><source>Tob. Control</source><year>1996</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>199</fpage><lpage>204</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9035354</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20-ijerph-06-00246"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rigotti</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Arnsten</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Mckool</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood-Reid</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Pasternak</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Smoking by patients in a smoke-free hospital: Prevalence, predictors, and implications</article-title><source>Prev. Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>159</fpage><lpage>166</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10938217</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21-ijerph-06-00246"><label>21.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Longo</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kruse</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Brownson</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hewett</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A prospective investigation of the impact of smoking bans on tobacco cessation and relapse</article-title><source>Tob. Control</source><year>2001</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>267</fpage><lpage>272</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11544392</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22-ijerph-06-00246"><label>22.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Offord</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurt</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Berge</surname><given-names>KG</given-names></name><name><surname>Frusti</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmidt</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of the implementation of a smoke-free policy in a medical center</article-title><source>Chest</source><year>1992</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>1531</fpage><lpage>1536</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1424878</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b23-ijerph-06-00246"><label>23.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Stahl</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ikle</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Grannis</surname><given-names>FW</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Employee attitudes and smoking behavior at the City of Hope National Medical Center smoke-free campus</article-tit